## Why This Is Asked
Assesses ability to turn path-based objectives into simple local transitions without extraneous state. The incremental gain depends only on adjacent cell values, enabling a clean DP.

## Key Concepts
- Grid DP with monotone moves
- Backpointers for path reconstruction
- Space optimization potential

## Code Example
```javascript
function maxAscents(grid){
  const n=grid.length, m=grid[0].length;
  const dp=Array.from({length:n}, ()=>Array(m).fill(0));
  const par=Array.from({length:n}, ()=>Array(m).fill(null));
  for(let i=0;i<n;i++){
    for(let j=0;j<m;j++){
      if(i===0 && j===0) continue;
      let top=-Infinity, left=-Infinity;
      if(i>0) top = dp[i-1][j] + (grid[i-1][j] < grid[i][j] ? 1:0);
      if(j>0) left = dp[i][j-1] + (grid[i][j-1] < grid[i][j] ? 1:0);
      if(top >= left){ dp[i][j] = top; par[i][j] = 'U'; } else { dp[i][j] = left; par[i][j] = 'L'; }
    }
  }
  // backtrack to build path
  return {score: dp[n-1][m-1], path: []};
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests DP partitioning with a non-sum objective and reconstruction requirements.

## Key Concepts
- DP over partitions with dp[i][t]
- Precomputing max-min for all subarrays
- Path reconstruction via parent pointers

## Code Example
```javascript
function maxMinSubarrayVal(arr){
  const n = arr.length;
  const maxVal = Array.from({length:n}, ()=>Array(n).fill(0));
  const minVal = Array.from({length:n}, ()=>Array(n).fill(0));
  for(let i=0;i<n;i++){
    let curMax = arr[i], curMin = arr[i];
    for(let j=i;j<n;j++){
      curMax = Math.max(curMax, arr[j]);
      curMin = Math.min(curMin, arr[j]);
      maxVal[i][j] = curMax;
      minVal[i][j] = curMin;
    }
  }
  const val = (l,r)=> maxVal[l][r] - minVal[l][r];
  return val;
}

function bestPartition(arr, k){
  const n = arr.length;
  const val = maxMinSubarrayVal(arr);
  const dp = Array.from({length:n+1}, ()=>Array(k+1).fill(-Infinity));
  const parent = Array.from({length:n+1}, ()=>Array(k+1).fill(-1));
  for(let i=1;i<=n;i++) dp[i][1] = val(0,i-1);
  for(let t=2;t<=k;t++){
    for(let i=t;i<=n;i++){
      for(let j=t-1;j<=i-1;j++){
        const cand = dp[j][t-1] + val(j, i-1);
        if(cand > dp[i][t]){ dp[i][t] = cand; parent[i][t]=j; }
      }
    }
  }
  // reconstruct
  let blocks = [];
  let i=n, t=k;
  while(t>0){
    const j = parent[i][t];
    blocks.push([j, i-1]);
    i = j; t--;
  }
  blocks.reverse();
  return {value: dp[n][k], blocks};
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How to optimize memory to O(nk)?
- Can you handle ties deterministically for block reconstruction?

## Why This Is Asked
This question tests proficiency with partition dynamic programming where subarrays must be non-overlapping and values derive from range statistics. The solution requires careful separation of concerns: precomputing range queries, implementing the DP transition, and reconstructing the solution through pointer tracking.

## Key Concepts
- Non-overlapping contiguous subarrays as partition elements
- Dynamic programming with two-dimensional state tracking
- Range minima preprocessing for O(1) query access
- Solution reconstruction through backpointers
- Complexity optimization through careful algorithm design

## Code Example
```javascript
function maxKSubarraysMin(A, k) {
  const n = A.length;

  // Precompute range minima
  const mins = Array.from({length: n}, () => Array(n).fill(0));
  for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) {
    let m = Infinity;
    for (let j = i; j < n; j++) {
      m = Math.min(m, A[j]);
      mins[i][j] = m;
    }
  }
```

## Why This Is Asked

Tests a non-trivial partition DP with a substring cost that requires precomputation and reconstruction, combining both combinatorial choices and an aggregate cost function.

## Key Concepts

- DP on partitions with a cost function over substrings
- Efficient precomputation of substring distinct counts
- Backtracking reconstruction of cut points
- Time/space trade-offs and memory optimization

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo: precompute cost[p][i], then DP with backpointers
const n = s.length;
const INF = 1e9;
const cost = Array.from({ length: n }, () => Array(n).fill(0));
for (let p = 0; p < n; p++) {
  const seen = new Array(26).fill(false);
  let distinct = 0;
  for (let i = p; i < n; i++) {
    const idx = s.charCodeAt(i) - 97;
    if (!seen[idx]) { seen[idx] = true; distinct++; }
    cost[p][i] = distinct;
  }
}
const kCap = Math.min(k, n);
const dp = Array.from({ length: n+1 }, () => Array(kCap+1).fill(INF));
const prv = Array.from({ length: n+1 }, () => Array(kCap+1).fill(-1));
dp[0][0] = 0;
for (let i = 1; i <= n; i++) {
  for (let t = 1; t <= Math.min(i, kCap); t++) {
    for (let p = t-1; p <= i-1; p++) {
      const cand = dp[p][t-1] + cost[p][i-1];
      if (cand < dp[i][t]) { dp[i][t] = cand; prv[i][t] = p; }
