## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to model multi-block dynamic programming with non-trivial block scoring that depends on range statistics (max, min) and block length. It also covers reconstruction of the exact blocks, and invites discussion of time/space trade-offs.

## Key Concepts

- Partition DP with fixed k blocks
- Block score uses range (max-min) and length
- Inline maintenance of max/min while expanding the last block
- Path reconstruction with predecessor pointers

## Code Example

```javascript
function maxScore(A, k) {
  const n = A.length;
  const NEG = -1e15;
  const dp = Array.from({length: n+1}, () => Array(k+1).fill(NEG));
  const parent = Array.from({length: n+1}, () => Array(k+1).fill(-1));

  dp[0][0] = 0;

  for (let i = 1; i <= n; i++) {
    for (let t = 1; t <= k; t++) {
      let curMax = -INF, curMin = INF;
      for (let l = i; l >= 1; l--) {
        curMax = Math.max(curMax, A[l-1]);
        curMin = Math.min(curMin, A[l-1]);
        const blockScore = (curMax - curMin) * (i - l + 1);
        if (dp[l-1][t-1] + blockScore > dp[i][t]) {
          dp[i][t] = dp[l-1][t-1] + blockScore;
          parent[i][t] = l-1;
        }
      }
    }
  }

  // Reconstruct blocks
  const blocks = [];
  let i = n, t = k;
  while (t > 0) {
    const l = parent[i][t] + 1;
    blocks.unshift([l, i]);
    i = l - 1;
    t--;
  }

  return {maxScore: dp[n][k], blocks};
}
```

## Time/Space Complexity

Time: O(n²k) - for each i and t, we scan O(n) possible l values while maintaining max/min.

Space: O(nk) for dp table plus O(nk) for parent pointers if reconstruction needed, otherwise O(nk).

## Why This Is Asked
This question tests building a DP over subsequences with constraints, requiring a clear state definition and transition over previous indices, plus reconstruction capabilities.

## Key Concepts
- Subsequence DP with constraints
- State dp[i] and parent tracking
- Time/space analysis and reconstruction

## Code Example
```javascript
function maxSubseqWithDiff(a, d) {
  const n = a.length;
  const dp = Array(n).fill(0);
  const par = Array(n).fill(-1);
  let best = -Infinity, bestIdx = -1;

  for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) {
    dp[i] = a[i];
    for (let j = 0; j < i; j++) {
      if (Math.abs(a[i] - a[j]) <= d && dp[j] + a[i] > dp[i]) {
        dp[i] = dp[j] + a[i];
        par[i] = j;
      }
    }
    if (dp[i] > best) {
      best = dp[i];
      bestIdx = i;
    }
  }

  // Reconstruct subsequence
  const seq = [];
  let curr = bestIdx;
  while (curr !== -1) {
    seq.push(curr);
    curr = par[curr];
  }
  return { maxSum: best, subsequence: seq.reverse() };
}
```

## Time/Space Complexity
Time: O(n²) due to nested loops checking all previous indices
Space: O(n) for dp and parent arrays
